'''''Phleum arenarium''''', the '''sand cat's tail''' or '''sand timothy''', is a species of flowering plant in the grass family [[Poaceae]].<ref name="RHS_235753" >{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/235753/phleum-arenarium/details |title=''Phleum arenarium'' sand cat's tail |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2026 |website=Find a plant |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=13 August 2026 |quote=1 suppliers }}</ref><ref name="EPPO_PHLAR" >{{cite web |url=https://gd.eppo.int/taxon/PHLAR |title=''Phleum arenarium'' (PHLAR) |author=<!--Not stated-->|date=2026 |website=EPPO Global Database |publisher=European and Mediterranean Plant Protection Organization |access-date=13 August 2026 |quote=Common names: sand catstail, English (GB); sand timothy, English (US) }}</ref> It is native to Europe, Morocco, and the Levant, and it has been introduced to a number of locales around the world; the U.S. states of Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, and Oregon, [[Primorsky Krai]], and Western Australia.<ref name="POWO_415780-1" >{{cite POWO |id=415780-1 |title=''Phleum arenarium'' L. |access-date=13 August 2026 }}</ref> An annual, it is typically found in coastal dunes and other sandy areas.<ref name="POWO_415780-1" /><ref name="1_of_1710_Google_Scholar_results" >{{cite journal |last1=Giovanni |first1=Sburlino |last2=Gabriella |first2=Buffa |last3=Leonardo |first3=Filesi |last4=U. |first4=Gamper |last5=L. |first5=Ghirelli |title=Phytocoenotic diversity of the N-Adriatic coastal sand dunes – the herbaceous communities of the fixed dunes and the vegetation of the interdunal wetlands |journal=Plant Sociology |date=2013 |volume=50 |issue=2 |doi=10.7338/pls2013502/04 }}</ref> It is occasionally available from commercial suppliers.<ref name="RHS_235753" />

